WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.563
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Thursday, November twelfth.

2
00:00:04.563 --> 00:00:13.803
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:13.803 --> 00:00:14.742
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.742 --> 00:00:31.501
Today: Houthi cruise missiles fired toward Riyadh, a reported Iranian attack on navigation systems on an Omani island, a deadly strike on a hospital in Gaza, a higher police death toll in northwest Pakistan, and Congo's Ebola outbreak still out of control after six months.

5
00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.349
We start with Saudi Arabia.

6
00:00:33.349 --> 00:00:39.118
Reuters reports Saudi air defenses intercepted three Houthi cruise missiles launched toward Riyadh.

7
00:00:39.118 --> 00:00:50.259
Al Jazeera reports the Houthis said they targeted King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh and a pumping station near Yanbu, and denied Saudi claims that they launched a drone toward Mecca.

8
00:00:50.259 --> 00:01:04.226
Arab News reports the Saudi led coalition also said it destroyed two ballistic missiles over the western region, two drones over the Mecca and southern regions, and another drone in the Riyadh area early today.

9
00:01:04.226 --> 00:01:06.466
Next, Oman.

10
00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:10.936
Reuters reports, citing sources, that Iran attacked shipping navigation systems on Oman's Didamar island.

11
00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:12.300
Turning to Gaza.

12
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:24.805
Reuters reports an Israeli airstrike on a building at Nasser Hospital in Khan Younis killed at least five people, including a surgeon, and wounded twenty others, a spokesman for Gaza's civil defense service said.

13
00:01:24.805 --> 00:01:30.050
The Associated Press, citing Gaza's Health Ministry, puts the death toll at six.

14
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:36.110
Al Jazeera reports the strike hit the surgery department and the intensive care unit.

15
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:38.777
In Pakistan, an update on the police ambush in Kohat.

16
00:01:38.777 --> 00:01:53.386
The Express Tribune, citing a Kohat police spokesperson, reports at least ten police officers, including a deputy superintendent, were killed when militants attacked a police team during an operation against illegal gold mining in the Gambat area.

17
00:01:53.386 --> 00:01:58.547
Tribal News Network reports eleven police were killed and eighteen attackers died.

18
00:01:58.547 --> 00:02:01.152
And in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.

19
00:02:01.152 --> 00:02:14.357
Reuters reports Doctors Without Borders says that six months into Congo's Ebola outbreak, many cases are likely being missed, transmission in hospitals in some areas is rife, and the virus is still spreading out of control.

20
00:02:14.357 --> 00:02:25.937
In an update from Kenya, Reuters reports the country has discharged its last Ebola patient, starting a forty two day countdown before it can be declared free of the disease, the health minister said.

21
00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:29.197
Now a few quick notes by region.

22
00:02:29.197 --> 00:02:40.688
In Asia, Australia's Smartraveller has lowered its advice for the flood affected areas of Rasuwa and Nuwakot districts in Nepal to exercise a high degree of caution, the same level as the rest of the country.

23
00:02:40.688 --> 00:02:54.232
Smartraveller also says to expect road closures and increased security for the ASEAN Summit in Manila from November sixteenth to eighteenth, and for APEC leaders' meetings in Shenzhen, China, on November eighteenth and nineteenth.

24
00:02:54.232 --> 00:03:10.241
In southern Thailand, The Nation reports roadside explosions damaged a school van in Satun yesterday, injuring three students, while electricity poles were attacked in Songkhla, and Thai public broadcaster M C O T reports arson and bomb attacks in Yala.

25
00:03:10.241 --> 00:03:20.694
In Europe, Reuters reports Russia and Ukraine exchanged attacks on each other's capitals early today, shortly before U.S. envoys arrived in Moscow to meet President Putin.

26
00:03:20.694 --> 00:03:24.749
Reuters also reports Romania's intelligence agency says it identified a Russian linked cyberattack.

27
00:03:24.749 --> 00:03:33.415
And an update on Italy: Reuters now reports around sixty three hundred schools received bomb warnings yesterday.

28
00:03:33.415 --> 00:03:41.766
In the Middle East, the Institute for the Study of War says Iran has formally abandoned its self imposed two thousand kilometer missile range limit.

29
00:03:41.766 --> 00:03:43.605
And the Critical Threats Project says the U.S.

30
00:03:43.605 --> 00:03:55.161
Justice Department on Tuesday, November tenth, indicted three members of an Iranian supported Kataib Hezbollah front group over nearly twenty attacks or plots in Europe and the United States.

31
00:03:55.161 --> 00:04:04.678
In Africa, the U.N. humanitarian office says suspected cholera and acute watery diarrhea cases are rising rapidly after floods in Mudug, Somalia.

32
00:04:04.678 --> 00:04:17.094
In eastern Congo, the local news site Kivu Morning Post reports four people were killed and seven houses burned in an attack attributed to the A D F rebels at Mabalako, in Beni territory; other local outlets put the toll at three.

33
00:04:17.094 --> 00:04:30.703
And Britain's Foreign Office has updated its travel advice for Madagascar with Ebola entry requirements and health screening, and for Liberia with heightened health screening for arriving travelers.

34
00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:36.538
In the Americas, InSight Crime reports a criminal group allegedly plotted to kill Christopher White, the mayor of San Bernardo, Chile.

35
00:04:36.538 --> 00:04:49.533
And in cyber, Microsoft says it observed threat actors deploying a tool called GSocket on compromised Linux servers to keep access after the original vulnerabilities were fixed.

36
00:04:49.533 --> 00:04:50.943
That's today's brief.

37
00:04:50.943 --> 00:04:59.293
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

38
00:04:59.293 --> 00:05:07.618
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

39
00:05:07.618 --> 00:05:09.879
This brief is digitally narrated.

40
00:05:09.879 --> 00:05:10.863
Questions?

41
00:05:10.863 --> 00:05:14.339
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

42
00:05:14.339 --> 00:05:16.632
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
